d like  she's cutting a piece of cake it's  interesting to see in this behind the  scenes photo which Henry Cavill posted  to his Instagram that the green prop  version still resembled ahead  later in the big Showdown after he  blocks Wonder Woman's attack Superman  pulls her arms apart and headbutts her  she fires one right back at him which  takes him a second to recover from after  he's had enough Superman delivers the  headbutt of all headbutts when he lifts  himself in the air and comes down on  Wonder Woman Like a ton of bricks in  order to get this scene perfect a green  screen covered crew member had to Aid  Henry Cavill by bending his legs in a  way which brought more fluidity to his  body while he was held up with wires it  would have been impossible for Cavill to  bend his body this way while up on the  wires so the silly looking crew member  was essential to get it just right  it turns out that one of the movie's key  outdoor scenes was actually filmed  outside if you can believe it after  Clark Kent sees Lois Lane and is  reminded of who he is the duo flies off  to his family's foreclosed farm and  spends some time in the field getting  reacquainted while the white farmhouse  was real the massive tree and  surrounding buildings we see in the  movie aren't large green screens were  used so additional buildings could be  added in as well as a few oversized  leafless trees we had seen these extra  buildings before in Man of Steel where  Clark's father Jonathan Kent hid his  crashed Kryptonian ship after the boy  first landed on Earth throughout Zack  Snyder's Justice League we see Bruce  Wayne Cyborg and Alfred work on the  Flying Fox the jet Bruce constructed as  a Troop Carrier the team had some issues  getting it to fly but eventually the jet  is in working order and carries the team  across the world to take on Steppenwolf  Bruce mans the Flying Fox alone after  dropping the team off on land and takes  down steppenwolf's force field allowing  everyone 