his film which was really great but  otherwise it's quite like an abstract  experience  when Angelina Jolie accepted the lead  role in Disney's Maleficent she brought  in her own personal makeup artist and a  special effects makeup Guru together  they created the anti-heroine's look  staying as close to the animated version  from 1959 Sleeping Beauty as possible  the crafted facial Prosthetics to give  Jolie those high cheekbones which  reportedly made execs at The Mouse House  rather nervous Ariane Titan the makeup  artist who created said facial  Prosthetics told fashionista they were  like wait what Prosthetics on Angelina  why are we covering Iraq they were not  very keen on it Jolie insisted on  keeping them and ultimately got her way  but the movie still utilized plenty of  visual effects after all this is a  fantasy movie featuring some major  action sequences the kind of scenes that  can only be achieved with CGI according  to Kelly Port the movie's VFX supervisor  he and his team decided to adopt a less  is more approach which paid off  handsomely he says for me visual effects  are a tool and should always be thought  of as a tool to support the film they  always need to serve the purpose of the  film and move the story along that's  when there are most successful with  Maleficent we knew what was working well  and what to pay attention to  according to NPC's Jessica Norman Disney  wanted the latest in visual effects for  2019's Maleficent Mistress of evil there  were over a thousand bfx artists working  on the big budget sequel at one stage  many of them pouring their time and  energy into Angelina Jolie's flying  sequences Norman told Art of bfx the  actress and the other fake characters  were filmed whilst attached to operated  tuning fork rigs on a blue screen stage  in some shots we attached CG Wings some  shots are full or partial CG takeovers  in a behind the scenes feature at Jolie  revealed what it's like being strapped  into a rotating toony Fork 